From dd0bc89d762bfb4e0a704c5abc53892eb4e279d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4: FP8 quantize-dequantize of the attention output
 before wo_a (1017)

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017's reference code rounds the attention output o
to FP8 (blocks of 32 along each group's row, power-of-two scales) and
back before the wo_a einsum, in the attention and in the DSpark draft's
attention; its weights expect it. SGLANG_DSV4_O_FP8_QDQ_BLOCK=<n> turns
the step on for the bf16 wo_a path (0 or unset: as before); the public
repo's launcher reads n from the checkpoint's own inference/model.py, so
the earlier release keeps it off.

The kernel is an in-place Triton quantize-dequantize, bit-exact against
the checkpoint's tilelang act_quant; GPUs older than sm89 get an fp32
emulation of the e4m3 rounding, also bit-exact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g
